    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (78.42) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) are our clear offensive pillars. **James Wood** benefits from an elite combination of a high-ceiling matchup against Brandon Young and a favorable park factor, while **Mickey Moniak** capitalizes on a high-upside encounter with Mike Paredes. Both players are well-positioned to drive our runs and power totals. Additionally, **Jose Caballero** (62.42) provides a sneaky high-floor play today; despite a lower base projection, his massive +13% dynamic platoon edge against Bennett, combined with a high likelihood of a stolen base opportunity against a slow-delivery pitcher, makes him a priority start in our MI slot.\n\nThe optimizer faced its toughest decision regarding the final utility spot, ultimately settling on **Kyle Karros** (51.16) over **Zach McKinstry** (47.14). While both players possess comparable raw projections, **Kyle Karros** was favored due to the specific matchup volatility of Mike Paredes, which offers more potential for a multi-hit performance than the matchup against Teng. We are closely monitoring the lineup status for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Alex Freeland**, **Austin Riley**, **Henry Bolte**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Corbin Carroll**; should any of these players be moved down in their respective batting orders or rested, we have sufficient coverage, but their high-leverage positions are currently baked into their projected efficiency.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the density of \"Lineup Pending\" statuses across the board. We are particularly concerned with **Austin Riley** (48.28), who draws the short straw against the elite Logan Webb. While his wind-out projection offers a slight boost, he faces the dual threat of a difficult arm and an elite defensive catcher. We are keeping **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Max Muncy** on high alert on the bench; while neither cracked the starting lineup today, their platoon profiles would make them immediate insertions should late lineup changes affect **Seiya Suzuki** or **Gabriel Moreno**. We continue to manage our bench depth\u2014including **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana**\u2014to ensure we maximize our game caps while maintaining our edge in the scarce stolen base category.",
